{
  "$comment": "The one status word every surface shows (T-0583). The adapter decides it (aura_adapter/status.py status_word) and sends it as `status: {word, reason}` in GET /api/status; the console, the phone and the desktop print `label` from that field and decide nothing themselves. `precedence` is the order the adapter tests in: the first that holds gives the reason. An unloaded model at rest is ready: llama-swap unloads it most of the evening. `no_answer` is the one label a surface produces itself, when the request to the adapter fails. Read by aura-adapter/tests, jarvis-web status.test.ts, the phone's HermesStatusTest and aura-desktop/tests.",
